{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e","id":936031,"title":"Blood Bonds 2E","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-23T05:09:13-07:00","id":936031,"title":"Blood Bonds 2E","content":"In the 2nd Edition of Vampire: The Requiem, when you built up Blood Bonds you need to drink from someone for 3 consecutive days? I mean can a Kindred feed another one 3 times his blood and then create a 3rd stage Blood Bond on the same night?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11988-montgomery-crobes","name":"Montgomery Crobes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T05:24:04-07:00","id":936037,"title":"","content":"According to the developers, blood bonds do not need to be formed over multiple nights. It needs to be three different <i>drinks</i>, but it can all happen in a single night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T07:55:00-07:00","id":936084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936037#post936037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to the developers, blood bonds do not need to be formed over multiple nights. It needs to be three different <i>drinks</i>, but it can all happen in a single night.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reference on that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T08:59:37-07:00","id":936106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936037#post936037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to the developers, blood bonds do not need to be formed over multiple nights. It needs to be three different <i>drinks</i>, but it can all happen in a single night.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am almost 100% positive that there is a thread out here that the developers stated that it had to be 3 nights. 1 stage per night. I thought it was in the FAQ but it's not there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T09:17:05-07:00","id":936109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936106#post936106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am almost 100% positive that there is a thread out here that the developers stated that it had to be 3 nights. 1 stage per night. I thought it was in the FAQ but it's not there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T09:23:26-07:00","id":936113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936109#post936109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div> I am sorry. I do not understand your comment? Same thing .. as?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T09:49:54-07:00","id":936126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936113#post936113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I am sorry. I do not understand your comment? Same thing .. as?</div> </div> </div> </div>Same thing as what you said. He's agreeing with you that he thought he remembered such a thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T09:54:09-07:00","id":936127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936084#post936084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reference on that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 100:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Any time a character imbibes a point or more of Vitae, it creates or reinforces a blood bond. The bond comes in three stages, usually at the first, second, and third drinks. </div> </div> </div>The phrasing &quot;<i>any time</i> the character imbibes a point or more of Vitae&quot;, with no stipulation about the times needing to be on separate nights seems clear as crystal to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T09:57:20-07:00","id":936128,"title":"","content":"I wish I could find that thread. I know I posted it ( or at least in it ) Because I was doing any time in one of my games and I had a player just all willy nilly blood bonding humans 3rd stage. I thought it was too OP and I very distinctly remember getting told 1 stage per night and saying to myself &quot;oh shit I have been doing this wrong&quot; <br /> <br /> Asked a friend who seems to remember that thread too. He also pointed out that dot 3 of coil of the voivode would be pointless if you can 3 stages in 1 night. It costs 5 vitae to 3 stage blood bond over a few minutes.. Why would you spend 5 if you only needed 3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":".  Added stuff 07-23-2016, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T11:41:09-07:00","id":936171,"title":"","content":"In VtM it has to be on 3 different nights ... In Requiem it doesn\u00b4t seem to have to be on 3 different nights. ...Probably 3 feedings of each 1 point (~ 500ml) with some time (maybe 1 hour???) in between would be sufficient to create a blood bond 3. <br /> <br /> ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11546-christoph","name":"Christoph+","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T11:50:10-07:00","id":936177,"title":"","content":"The one stage per night was reinforced in 1st edition Requiem with the short story of Loki trapping his father in a full vinculum over three different nights. I also recall reading on one of the forums that a vampire could only do one stage per scene per person but multiple scenes can take place in a single night. But yes, if you can ram a 3 stage vinculum down someone's throat in a single scene by having them take three sips of a drink or bites of food contaminated by a single vitae, that does render the voivode coil completely worthless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T12:08:55-07:00","id":936182,"title":"","content":"I don\u00b4t know how you handle it, bu if a human has 10 blood points and 5 L blood in his body, then 1 bp should be 0,5 L ... That\u00b4s far more than a &quot;sip&quot; .... In VtM was it only a sip ....<br /> <br /> I\u00b4m wondering how much vitae a mortal could drink if he would have unlimited access... ?<br /> <br /> An adult stomach as a maximum volume of 3-4 L ... But as far as I can tell, 2 L of liquid would be my maxium (I\u00b4m a tall man).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11546-christoph","name":"Christoph+","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T13:11:10-07:00","id":936203,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't worry too much about volume. You are using Vitae, not blood. One Blood-point is the lowest amount of Vitae to be relevant, and need not be a 1:1 in volume with blood.<br /> <br /> Not sure if that is a house rule or if I read it somewhere. It does account for Vitae from different sources however, e.g Cows.<br /> <br /> All you lose as a trade off is the massive explosion of blood from blowing up an Elder. :P<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T13:57:39-07:00","id":936227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christoph+</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936182#post936182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u00b4t know how you handle it, bu if a human has 10 blood points and 5 L blood in his body, then 1 bp should be 0,5 L ... That\u00b4s far more than a &quot;sip&quot; .... In VtM was it only a sip ....<br /> <br /> I\u00b4m wondering how much vitae a mortal could drink if he would have unlimited access... ?<br /> <br /> An adult stomach as a maximum volume of 3-4 L ... But as far as I can tell, 2 L of liquid would be my maxium (I\u00b4m a tall man).</div> </div> </div> </div>What you're failing to grasp is that vitae is more a measure of stolen life-force than actual blood made more viscous by some internal vampiric process in their dead organs. Otherwise, an elder with capacity for 100 points of vitae in his system would be a bloated abomination instead of a humanoid-shaped monster.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the calculation is innacurate: A vampire can drain as much vitae from a single human as twice their health. 1 point of lethal damage per vitae taken, done twice per size and stamina = filled track with aggravated damage and a dead human.<br /> <br /> Also, no, that doesn't leaves a body completely bereft of blood. The Masquerade wouldn't hold much at all with the advent of autopsies if that was the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T14:15:28-07:00","id":936238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936227#post936227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> Furthermore, the calculation is innacurate: A vampire can drain as much vitae from a single human as twice their health. 1 point of lethal damage per vitae taken, done twice per size and stamina = filled track with aggravated damage and a dead human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately this is inaccurate too. If a human has 8 health, a vampire can take 8 vitae. You can take as much vitae as your victim has health dots. <br /> Size+stamina= the vitae you can take. Not once for lethal and once for aggravated, it's just once. <br /> <br /> There is a huge huge thread about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T14:26:37-07:00","id":936242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936238#post936238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unfortunately this is inaccurate too. If a human has 8 health, a vampire can take 8 vitae. You can take as much vitae as your victim has health dots.<br /> Size+stamina= the vitae you can take. Not once for lethal and once for aggravated, it's just once.<br /> <br /> There is a huge huge thread about this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Link please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T14:35:38-07:00","id":936246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936242#post936242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Link please?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/811316-estimating-stamina\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...mating-stamina</a><br /> <br /> Found that one! <br /> <br /> The book says &quot;dots&quot;. Too but I can't find pages on my phone","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T14:43:28-07:00","id":936249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936106#post936106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am almost 100% positive that there is a thread out here that the developers stated that it had to be 3 nights. 1 stage per night. I thought it was in the FAQ but it's not there.</div> </div> </div> </div> Nope. You're thinking of 1e. Its no longer true. No where is it mentioned in a thread, the book, or a FAQ that it requires three nights. There was a thread a while back where people swore up and down that it took three nights, but there was never any dev or writer who supported that stance.<br /> <br /> Now, the developers have said that a large number of vampires <i>believe</i> that it takes three nights to gain a full Vinculum. But vampires believe a lot of things about their Curse that aren't true. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T14:48:49-07:00","id":936253,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2\" data-vbnamecard=\"2\">Rose Bailey</a> So, which is it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T14:52:33-07:00","id":936258,"title":"","content":"If it doesn't take 3 nights it makes the 3rd dot of the coil pointless and overly expensive. So I would like a developer to clarify too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T15:08:35-07:00","id":936265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936128#post936128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish I could find that thread. I know I posted it ( or at least in it ) Because I was doing any time in one of my games and I had a player just all willy nilly blood bonding humans 3rd stage. I thought it was too OP and I very distinctly remember getting told 1 stage per night and saying to myself &amp;quot;oh shit I have been doing this wrong&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If you do find it, let me know. I'd be interested to see what was said there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936128#post936128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Asked a friend who seems to remember that thread too. He also pointed out that dot 3 of coil of the voivode would be pointless if you can 3 stages in 1 night. It costs 5 vitae to 3 stage blood bond over a few minutes.. Why would you spend 5 if you only needed 3?</div> </div> </div> </div>What Voivode allows you do is to reduce the number of times the subject needs to drink your Vitae by increasing the amount. Bleed 5 Vitae into someone's wine glass and you've got them in a 3rd stage bond. Without it, you can pour 100 Vitae into that wine, it's still only one instance of drinking &quot;one or more&quot; Vitae, and you still need to find a way to get them to drink your Vitae two more times if you want a 3rd stage bond.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T18:12:08-07:00","id":936330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936258#post936258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it doesn't take 3 nights it makes the 3rd dot of the coil pointless and overly expensive. So I would like a developer to clarify too.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not at all. The Coil lets you establish a full vinculum with a single drink - and that's a bigger deal that you think. Being fed on in combat? Trying to feed someone else forcefully in combat? Trading a single drink for a signature Discipline? Reviving a vampire from torpor? Targetted by rogue ghouls / Ashwood Abby addicts? Diablarist after you? Limited time to feed someone you've caught in a Discipline for the moment?<br /> <br /> There are lots of situations where feeding people once comes up. And this lets you basically trap anyone into a full bond with &quot;a single sip.&quot; Call to Serve isn't bound by the vitae/turn limits either, so its basically a split-second decision to use it at its full potential and with the smallest drop of vitae. This lets you skip a lot of steps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T03:17:05-07:00","id":936479,"title":"","content":"so, what you say that it is possible to create a blood Bond just by putting some drops into someone's glass of wine?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11546-christoph","name":"Christoph+","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T05:55:10-07:00","id":936508,"title":"","content":"A vampire can spit in your eye and establish a vinculum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T06:54:03-07:00","id":936521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christoph+</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936479#post936479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so, what you say that it is possible to create a blood Bond just by putting some drops into someone's glass of wine?</div> </div> </div> </div>That particular point is a matter of some contention. I would say yes, but some folks think the Vitae would become inert if out of the vampire's body for even a minute, and therefore wouldn't establish a blood bond.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T06:55:02-07:00","id":936523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936508#post936508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A vampire can spit in your eye and establish a vinculum.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you figure?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T07:01:22-07:00","id":936525,"title":"","content":"I believe it was a Masquerade book, but there's a story about a Nosferatu who spat into a person's eye and that person became a ghoul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T09:08:21-07:00","id":936563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936523#post936523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you figure?</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 60 of Blood and Smoke describes several ways for vampires to create vinculums and ghouls besides feeding vitae to a willing recipient from their wrist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T09:35:19-07:00","id":936580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936563#post936563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 60 of Blood and Smoke describes several ways for vampires to create vinculums and ghouls besides feeding vitae to a willing recipient from their wrist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Edit: nevermind, I see what you were referencing. It's actually on page 59 though, so that was confusing. Remember, PDF page numbers are all 1 off from physical page numbers because PDFs count the cover as page 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-24-2016, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T10:40:25-07:00","id":936609,"title":"","content":"It says that you can do the vitae over several turns to make it count as 1 sip. <br /> <br /> You would have to have 5 BP to be able to spill that much blood in one turn wouldn't you? <br /> <br /> If you are lower BP as can't spill 5 in one turn why wouldn't you do 5 rolls for the 5 drinks ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T10:43:25-07:00","id":936610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936609#post936609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It says that you can do the vitae over several turns to make it count as 1 sip. <br /> <br /> You would have to have 5 BP to be able to spill that much blood in one turn wouldn't you? <br /> <br /> If you are lower BP as can't spill 5 in one turn why wouldn't you do 5 rolls for the 5 drinks ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would anyone accept 5 drinks from you after the first one tasted like blood?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T10:57:09-07:00","id":936617,"title":"","content":"While you do need to spend points of Vitae to feed a ghoul, I never thought you needed more than an uncounted-for fraction of a Vitae to blood bond. Has everyone else been doing it differently, where a full Vitae point is used to blood bond?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T11:49:21-07:00","id":936636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936617#post936617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While you do need to spend points of Vitae to feed a ghoul, I never thought you needed more than an uncounted-for fraction of a Vitae to blood bond. Has everyone else been doing it differently, where a full Vitae point is used to blood bond?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, in my understanding even a single drop/smear of vitae is enough for the blood bond (also for triggering vitae addiction).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4035-lepaca","name":"Lepaca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4035_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T12:00:03-07:00","id":936643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936609#post936609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It says that you can do the vitae over several turns to make it count as 1 sip.<br /> <br /> You would have to have 5 BP to be able to spill that much blood in one turn wouldn't you?<br /> <br /> If you are lower BP as can't spill 5 in one turn why wouldn't you do 5 rolls for the 5 drinks ?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;This Vitae must be shared over no more than a few minutes, but is not subject to limits on Vitae per turn.&quot; Voivode 3 is not subject to vitae/turn limits. So, you can have BP 1 and use that much <i>vitae</i> in a single turn. Blood is a vector for the mystical force of vitae, but there's no guidelines on how much blood can contain how much vitae. A single drop could very well contain 5 vitae worth, especially when we're talking about Dragons. <br /> <br /> You can have a long drink that lasts a few minutes, or a short, quick gulp. It all depends on what is currently appropriate from a story perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T12:03:38-07:00","id":936648,"title":"","content":"That's how I do it and how I always played it. Basically saying you have to use enough vitae for your victim to taste. I dont feel like dealing with anal retentive rules lawyers having their character running around with syringes and hypodermic needles just to measure out enough to blood bond someone but still keep the vitae. That way I can also say surreptitiously allowing vitae to seep on your fingers while you mix a drink without it being visibly obvious counts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T12:56:45-07:00","id":936677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936617#post936617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While you do need to spend points of Vitae to feed a ghoul, I never thought you needed more than an uncounted-for fraction of a Vitae to blood bond. Has everyone else been doing it differently, where a full Vitae point is used to blood bond?</div> </div> </div> </div>The wording on the Blood Bond rules is &quot;any time a character imbibes a point or more of Vitae&quot;, so yeah, I rule that at least one point has to be expended. That said, the way I run it, there's no specific quantity of blood required to equal a full point of Vitae. You can do it with just a drop of blood or whatever, as long as you spend at least one point from the Vitae track on your character sheet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T17:31:28-07:00","id":936819,"title":"","content":"Eh. For regular blood bonding I just allow it as a natural ability like a werewolf's shapechange. Providing the vampire has some method to draw blood, fangs obviously counting, then I don't see why a drop should count a point of Vitae. Though I've never had to deal with tsusasi's players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T17:36:58-07:00","id":936820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936819#post936819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. For regular blood bonding I just allow it as a natural ability like a werewolf's shapechange. Providing the vampire has some method to draw blood, fangs obviously counting, then I don't see why a drop should count a point of Vitae. Though I've never had to deal with tsusasi's players.</div> </div> </div> </div>It should count for a point of Vitae because a point of Vitae is what the rules specifically call for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T19:54:56-07:00","id":936865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936610#post936610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would anyone accept 5 drinks from you after the first one tasted like blood?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vitae is not blood. Vitae is the most addictive substance in wod. After the first one they could be a total addict... Why wouldn't they continue to drink it if it is more addictive than say... Ecstasy? <br /> <br /> I would still like a developer's thoughts on the matter. <br /> I swear( though I can't find it ) that the powers that be said it was once a night. <br /> Not once a night would make 3rd dot ... Not as good, or at least confusing on why you would want to use it. <br /> <br /> If you can continue to give them<br /> Vitae over several minutes an have it count as one sip... Why would you not just make them roll and roll and get more and more and more addicted ?<br /> <br /> Come to think of it. Humans can't even resist the bond so it would only take 3 vitae to fully bond them in one night. ( how you make them drink it is up to you. ) <br /> <br /> A vampire would have a chance to resist. The roll would come at a cumulative negative. It takes a will power to try to resist, if I am not mistaking. It's super addictive. <br /> <br /> <br /> Roll -1 <br /> ( addict roll)<br /> Roll -2 <br /> ( addict roll )<br /> Roll -3<br /> (Addict roll )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 07-24-2016, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T20:24:18-07:00","id":936895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936865#post936865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vitae is not blood. Vitae is the most addictive substance in wod. After the first one they could be a total addict... Why wouldn't they continue to drink it if it is more addictive than say... Ecstasy?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Vitae is not blood, but it is borne by blood, which means if you want to add Vitae to someone's drink, you need to bleed into it and that's going to make it taste weird. Yes, Vitae is addictive, but it is not the most addictive substance in CofD (the book compares it to &quot;a powerful drug&quot;, so it is likely on par with ecstasy), and addiction is far from guaranteed, especially when only a small amount is imbibed. The subject gets a resistance roll. If they fail that, they can still make a roll to resist an offer of more. If they fail that, they can <i>still</i> refuse the offer at the cost of taking the Deprived Condition, which anyone who knows about blood bonds is likely to do rather than risk being bonded.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936865#post936865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would still like a developer's thoughts on the matter. <br /> I swear( though I can't find it ) that the powers that be said it was once a night.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been looking too. Haven't found the thread yet, but if I do I'll let you know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936865#post936865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not once a night makes 3rd dot ... Not as good, or at least confusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It lets you ignore the Vitae/turn limit for the purposes of bonding people, and it lets you get a third stage bond in one drink instead of having to get them to drink three separate times. That's fantastic if you want to bond someone who doesn't want to be bonded.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936865#post936865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you can continue to give them<br /> Vitae over several minutes an have it count as one sip... Why would you not just make them roll and roll and get more and more and more addicted ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand what you mean by this. Can you rephrase?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T20:41:10-07:00","id":936900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936895#post936895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, Vitae is not blood, but it is borne by blood, which means if you want to add Vitae to someone's drink, you need to bleed into it and that's going to make it taste weird. Yes, Vitae is addictive, but it is not the most addictive substance in CofD (the book compares it to &quot;a powerful drug&quot;, so it is likely on par with ecstasy), and addiction is far from guaranteed, especially when only a small amount is imbibed. The subject gets a resistance roll. If they fail that, they can still make a roll to resist an offer of more. If they fail that, they can <i>still</i> refuse the offer at the cost of taking the Deprived Condition, which anyone who knows about blood bonds is likely to do rather than risk being bonded.<br /> <br /> <br /> I've been looking too. Haven't found the thread yet, but if I do I'll let you know.<br /> <br /> <br /> It lets you ignore the Vitae/turn limit for the purposes of bonding people, and it lets you get a third stage bond in one drink instead of having to get them to drink three separate times. That's fantastic if you want to bond someone who doesn't want to be bonded.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't understand what you mean by this. Can you rephrase?</div> </div> </div> </div> The coil says that you can give them vitae over several minutes and make it count as one sip. Right? <br /> <br /> Tons of drugs can be slipped into drinks or what not and people don't notice. If it makes you feel as hopped up as coke or heroine or ecstasy, are you going to care your drink tasted off?? <br /> <br /> I realized I was unclear and added to original post. Sorry.<br /> <br /> Why not instead of 1 roll at -5 ( and only if you are a vampire ) to resist the blood bond, have them roll multiple times? Progressively getting worse? <br /> <br /> Humans can't resist it anyway. So why not just spend 3 instead of 5? The more you make them roll the more likely they will become addicted and bonded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 07-24-2016, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T20:58:31-07:00","id":936907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936900#post936900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The coil says that you can give them vitae over several minutes and make it count as one sip. Right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you talking about the part that says &quot;This Vitae must be shared over no more than a few minutes, but is not subject to limits on Vitae per turn.&quot;? That's a proscription. It <i>has to</i> be done over a few minutes <i>at most</i> to count as one drink. The point is to reduce the number of times you have to get the victim to drink from you to get to a third stage bond.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936900#post936900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tons of drugs can be slipped into drinks or what not and people don't notice. If it makes you feel as hopped up as coke or heroine or ecstasy, are you going to care your drink tasted off??</div> </div> </div> </div>Most drugs don't taste like blood, though. And if you know the person who offered you a drink is capable of making you a slave to their will if you drink their blood three times, and the drink tastes like blood, you're probably not going to want to drink stuff they offer you any more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936900#post936900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I realized I was unclear and added to original post. Sorry.<br /> <br /> Why not instead of 1 roll at -5 ( and only if you are a vampire ) to resist the blood bond, have them roll multiple times? Progressively getting worse? <br /> <br /> Humans can't resist it anyway. So why not just spend 3 instead of 5? The more you make them roll the more likely they will become addicted and bonded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but in order to do that you have to actually get them to drink your blood three times instead of just one time. Which takes time and is hard to actually do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T21:47:49-07:00","id":936920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Blood bearing Vitae is slightly darker, and has an almost<br /> syrupy quality. It has all the normal metallic smells blood<br /> should, but also has a subtle, sweet smell, like a dessert wine. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vitae is life. Life tastes very, very good. In fact, it tastes so<br /> good, it\u2019s highly addictive to both mortal and Kindred alike. </div> </div> </div>pg 98 and 99.<br /> <br /> So it doesn't taste like blood, but it smells mostly like blood, and it looks a whole lot like blood, and no matter what it decidedly does <i>not</i> taste or smell or look like whatever you put it into.<br /> <br /> And since someone brought it up:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cold blood from a corpse or kept outside the body for<br /> more than a few minutes (but no more than a night) </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Stored Kindred Vitae is effectively cold blood. </div> </div> </div>pg 95.<br /> <br /> I'm one of the folks that thinks you probably can't dose food or drink with it in the first place without it losing its potency. Admittedly, they don't fully define &quot;stored&quot; here, so it's up to ST interpretation. But there are easier ways, anyway. Obfuscate yourself and wait for the target to go to sleep. Pour it directly into their mouth. Majesty or Dominate them into drinking it. Force them if you're a physical sort of vampire. Get creative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T02:36:11-07:00","id":936987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936865#post936865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you not just make them roll and roll and get more and more and more addicted ?</div> </div> </div> </div> because addiction is not mind control. A one stage bond is not enough to control someone. People can resist addictions, especially when its so fresh, after all. <br /> <br /> Also, time and place might not allow it. Ideal circumstances are rare. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936920#post936920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it doesn't taste like blood, but it smells mostly like blood, and it looks a whole lot like blood, and no matter what it decidedly does <i>not</i> taste or smell or look like whatever you put it into.</div> </div> </div> </div> page 59 suggests that vitae still tastes of coppery metal. Which, for all intents and purposes, tastes close enough to be identified as blood. Or some iron-infested water. Definitely makes the drink you pour the vitae into tastes strange, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm one of the folks that thinks you probably can't dose food or drink with it in the first place without it losing its potency. </div> </div> </div> Putting vitae into coffee is one of the ways to make a ghoul, as per page 59. So, that one is kind of hard to get around without houserules. Though, time may still be a factor as the vitae breaks down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T05:24:13-07:00","id":937012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936920#post936920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> pg 98 and 99.<br /> <br /> So it doesn't taste like blood, but it smells mostly like blood, and it looks a whole lot like blood, and no matter what it decidedly does <i>not</i> taste or smell or look like whatever you put it into.<br /> <br /> And since someone brought it up:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> pg 95.<br /> <br /> I'm one of the folks that thinks you probably can't dose food or drink with it in the first place without it losing its potency. Admittedly, they don't fully define &amp;quot;stored&amp;quot; here, so it's up to ST interpretation. But there are easier ways, anyway. Obfuscate yourself and wait for the target to go to sleep. Pour it directly into their mouth. Majesty or Dominate them into drinking it. Force them if you're a physical sort of vampire. Get creative.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you that it's subtle and tastes sweet as per the book. I don't think someone would know. If it was put in a glass of wine as it tastes like wine. Drinks or food or needles of whatever I think would work. <br /> <br /> Strange tasting doesn't always equate bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T06:25:12-07:00","id":937039,"title":"","content":"No one said that vitae had to taste bad. The question is if it tastes enough like blood (not exactly like blood, but something similar) to be identifiable by those in the know (ie ghouls, hunters, blood dolls, touchstones, etc). Or if there's enough of a taste difference that someone might suspect that their drink was spiked (a big concern in modern day).<br /> <br /> Given what's on page 59, it seems to hint that, yes, there's a bit of a taste difference that the unsuspecting might not key in on. They don't recognize that its a problem, but its a nagging detail that the wary might catch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-25-2016, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T11:31:10-07:00","id":937186,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it doesn't really matter if it tastes like blood specifically, or if it tastes good or bad or what ever. What matters is that it tastes different from what the person drinking it expects, potentially arousing suspicion and making them not want to drink stuff you give them because they don't want to be supernaturally roofied.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T12:37:00-07:00","id":937224,"title":"","content":"I am not trying to argue for the sake of arguing (and now that I can get to a book and paste some references in I am going to ) but I feel that some points need some clarification. Doing one thing causes another. lots of cause and effects here...<br /> <br /> One of the arguments is that someone who had a spiked drink or food or whatever, Would not want to continue to drink or eat food because it tastes like coppery blood So it really does matter what it tastes like. most people do not turn down really really good tasting things.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot; <b>Vitae is life. Life tastes very, very good. In fact, it tastes so<br /> good, </b>it\u2019s highly addictive to both mortal and Kindred alike.<br /> Vitae\u2019s addictive quality is one of the strongest tools Kindred can<br /> bring to bear. Even ignoring the blood bond (see p. 90), Vitae<br /> is a remarkable bargaining chip. Just as in the mortal world,<br /> addiction\u2019s a terrible thing when leveraged against a person. &quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> If someone handed you a drink and you never had it before and it was the best thing you have ever tasted, strange or not. Why would you say no to round two? So sip 1. they have now had to roll for addiction ( vampire and mortal alike ) Human they are blood bonded ( which means they like you at least a little now, which would make them <i>more likely</i> to take round 2 ) If they are a vampire they are Kindred they have to spend a willpower to roll to not get bonded at negative per vitae consumed.<br /> <br /> So potential to become addicted and bonded in one go is ok, but chances are that you will be able to persuade your person to take another drink/bite. Considering how many potential negatives for resisting the addiction ( any time you are faced with it, you have to roll not to ) and the + they might have for the Blood bond in the social maneuvering.<br /> <br /> You do it again. there is that second roll at even a greater negative to not become bonded ( again, only if you are a vampire ) and even more of a negative to not be addicted. Rinse and repeat. the negatives for you are getting worse and worse as you go.<br /> <br /> I know that addiction is not mind control in anyway but you do have to roll a resolve comp NOT to take the drug again. So many rolls are happening for this and there are so many ways other than a drink. Here are some examples from the book ( this is specifically for ghouling, but also applies to addiction and bonding ) At best I would give the victim a perception check to notice something off, but with how good it is suppose to taste, I dont know that they would say no based off odd.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot; A vampire need not press the prospective ghoul\u2019s lips to<br /> his wrist. <b>There are so many other ways to skin that cat.</b><br /> The Serpent bites his lip, and you barely notice the copper<br /> in the kiss.<br /> The Haunt spits bloody phlegm in your eye, inexplicably, as<br /> you pass on the midnight road. Now you sit in your apartment<br /> feeling more afraid than you think you ought to, wondering<br /> if you should go get tested for some disease.<br /> You reach for your expensive coffee, but it tastes weird. A<br /> Shadow smiles in front of your face, but you cannot see her.<br /> You drank from a chalice when a Lord commanded you to.<br /> And now you\u2026no\u2026you don\u2019t quite remember what happened.<br /> The Savage cuts you and then herself, pressing the open<br /> wounds together. Something wild surges between. &quot; </i><br /> <br /> <br /> All that said. Many people seem to think that your victim will know what is happening to them. They seem to know that they are drinking vitae. I would only give another vampire, ghoul, or someone in the know an occult(maybe science?) roll to know that, but by then It might be too late. Considering the ratio Humans to vampires, most of your possible victims shouldnt even be aware that there is a chance to be supernaturally roofied.<br /> <br /> I am not saying that in some circumstances getting more than 1 drink is hard. I am saying that getting someone to do it 3 times isnt as hard as one might think it is. spending 3 vitae on a human to bond them seems a lot better than 5 and I think that situations where you know you can only get 1 drink are more rare than convincing someone to take 3.<br /> <br /> So you might lay out 5 shots and have them do 5 shots.. but why wouldn't you do 3 shots if they will have the same effect? Yes, I understand that sometimes 5 is needed, but 3 seems better all around. I also understand that is my perspective.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Is there anything else in WoD that makes you roll upon first taste to not be addicted? In college, took a class about OTC and Illegal drugs and the only drug ( that I remember.. it's been a while ) that you could get addicted to after the first hit was Ecstasy. Even heroine and Meth take repeated use... So if we equate vitae to the most addictive drug humans know... The only thing I can think of in wod that is more addicting... is Kiss of the Succubus..<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Araknee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/133323-advice-blood-bonding-the-torpid?p=133486#post133486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember that somewhere in the forum, Rose maked the point that it was <i>three different nights</i>, where a &quot;night&quot; was considered to be a new awakening that required 1 point of vitae.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=636690#post636690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ingesting few drops on first night, few drops on second, and in three nights vampires made rest of their starting group ( with Supernatural Advantages 1 ) loving him slaves.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Audrey St. John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/133323-advice-blood-bonding-the-torpid?p=133492#post133492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes you can potentially blood bond someone while they are torpid. You can't ascertain whether or not it's successful until they're awake. You also can't override someone else's vinculum if they've been bonded to someone else (which may well be the case if they're Invictus.) Which again you can't ascertain until they're awake.<br /> It's storyteller's fiat as to how much time must pass between drinks. A short story involving Loki blood bonding his father corroborates three separate nights are required. But that can also be described as three separate scenes.</div> </div> </div> </div>( circle of the crone book )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/480785-confidante-and-two-step-blood-bonds?p=481316#post481316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is my opinion here, but I dont see why Confidante wouldnt allow for that. First if the victim of majesty isnt a vampire they would have no idea what drinking your blood would do to them so they would just think you are a freak. Not a breaking point. Second if they were a vampire, then with Majesty they wouldnt want to upset you so why would they say no? It's not physically going to get them killed or hurt them, they are just going to love you a little more permanently. They would still get the roll to resist the bond.<br /> <br /> OR! just fill your mouth with vitae and tell them to kiss you forcing them to take the vitae anyway ( it says in the book Daeva like to do that ) &quot;Kiss me&quot; is a far less of a threatening command than &quot;take a blood bond with me&quot;<br /> <br /> Just be aware that in the FAQ or another thread in here somewhere it says you can only get 1 stage of blood bond per night.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I couldnt find the 3 nights thing, but I did find a couple people referencing the post...<br /> <br /> Ephsy, myself and Elderand seem to recall it too. ( I do hope we arent all crazy )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 07-25-2016, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T14:02:01-07:00","id":937272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937224#post937224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not trying to argue for the sake of arguing (and now that I can get to a book and paste some references in I am going to ) but I feel that some points need some clarification. Doing one thing causes another. lots of cause and effects here...<br /> <br /> <i>&quot; <b>Vitae is life. Life tastes very, very good. In fact, it tastes so<br /> good, </b>it\u2019s highly addictive to both mortal and Kindred alike.<br /> Vitae\u2019s addictive quality is one of the strongest tools Kindred can<br /> bring to bear. Even ignoring the blood bond (see p. 90), Vitae<br /> is a remarkable bargaining chip. Just as in the mortal world,<br /> addiction\u2019s a terrible thing when leveraged against a person. &quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>So it has a very distinct taste that characters in the know should easily be able to recognize.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937224#post937224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the arguments is that someone who had a spiked drink or food or whatever, Would not want to continue to drink or eat food because it tastes like coppery blood So it really does matter what it tastes like. most people do not turn down really really good tasting things.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it doesn't matter if it tastes good or bad, because when something tastes different than you expect it to, that's going to arouse suspicion, even if it tastes good. At least, that's the case if you have a modicum of self-preservation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937224#post937224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If someone handed you a drink and you never had it before and it was the best thing you have ever tasted, strange or not. Why would you say no to round two? So sip 1. they have now had to roll for addiction ( vampire and mortal alike ) Human they are blood bonded ( which means they like you at least a little now, which would make them <i>more likely</i> to take round 2 ) If they are a vampire they are Kindred they have to spend a willpower to roll to not get bonded at negative per vitae consumed.</div> </div> </div> </div>If someone handed me a drink and I had never had it before, I wouldn't even drink it the first time unless it was someone I knew very well and trusted implicitly, because I have no interest in being drugged, thank you very much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937224#post937224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So potential to become addicted and bonded in one go is ok, but chances are that you will be able to persuade your person to take another drink/bite. Considering how many potential negatives for resisting the addiction ( any time you are faced with it, you have to roll not to ) and the + they might have for the Blood bond in the social maneuvering.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <b>strongly</b> disagree that chances are good you'll be able to persuade the person to take another drink, and you have not said anything to convince me otherwise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937224#post937224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do it again. there is that second roll at even a greater negative to not become bonded ( again, only if you are a vampire ) and even more of a negative to not be addicted. Rinse and repeat. the negatives for you are getting worse and worse as you go.</div> </div> </div> </div>So far the scenario you presented has me drinking zero times.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937224#post937224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that addiction is not mind control in anyway but you do have to roll a resolve comp NOT to take the drug again. So many rolls are happening for this and there are so many ways other than a drink. Here are some examples from the book ( this is specifically for ghouling, but also applies to addiction and bonding ) At best I would give the victim a perception check to notice something off, but with how good it is suppose to taste, I dont know that they would say no based off odd.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you have to succeed on a resolve + composure roll, take the Vitae again, <i>or take the Deprived Condition</i>. Anyone who knows the taste and properties of Vitae (which any vampire who wasn't embraced yesterday should, most ghouls should, a decent number of hunters should, and some occult-interested humans might) will take the third option if they don't want to<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937224#post937224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>&quot; A vampire need not press the prospective ghoul\u2019s lips to<br /> his wrist. <b>There are so many other ways to skin that cat.</b><br /> The Serpent bites his lip, and you barely notice the copper<br /> in the kiss.<br /> The Haunt spits bloody phlegm in your eye, inexplicably, as<br /> you pass on the midnight road. Now you sit in your apartment<br /> feeling more afraid than you think you ought to, wondering<br /> if you should go get tested for some disease.<br /> You reach for your expensive coffee, <b>but it tastes weird.</b> A<br /> Shadow smiles in front of your face, but you cannot see her.<br /> You drank from a chalice when a Lord commanded you to.<br /> And now you\u2026no\u2026you don\u2019t quite remember what happened.<br /> The Savage cuts you and then herself, pressing the open<br /> wounds together. Something wild surges between. &quot; </i></div> </div> </div> </div>I bolded a bit for emphasis there. And Voivode 3 allows that haunt to get you to a 3rd stage blood bond after spitting in your eye that first time instead of having to find two more occasions to do it. It allows the Shadow to get you to a 3rd stage bond after that first sip of coffee instead of having to find two more ways to trick you into drinking her blood while you're suspicious of what she put in your coffee. The Lord only has to command you to drink from the chalice once to get you to a 3rd stage bond instead of three times out of three different chalices. The savage can get you into a 3rd stage bond with that one contact, instead of having to do it twice more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937224#post937224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All that said. Many people seem to think that your victim will know what is happening to them. They seem to know that they are drinking vitae. I would only give another vampire, ghoul, or someone in the know an occult(maybe science?) roll to know that, but by then It might be too late. Considering the ratio Humans to vampires, most of your possible victims shouldnt even be aware that there is a chance to be supernaturally roofied.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because people who have reason to be suspicious are the people Voivode 3 is useful in helping you bond. If the subject is willing or completely oblivious, sure, it's not really necessary. But that's just not always the case. Sometimes you want to bond a rival's favored Ghoul to turn him against her. Sometimes you want to bond an elder to get a leg up on them. Sometimes you want to bind a hunter to get him off your back. These are the occasions when consolidating the number of times you need to get your vitae into their system can be extremely beneficial.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937224#post937224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not saying that in some circumstances getting more than 1 drink is hard. I am saying that getting someone to do it 3 times isnt as hard as one might think it is. spending 3 vitae on a human to bond them seems a lot better than 5 and I think that situations where you know you can only get 1 drink are more rare than convincing someone to take 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, but that doesn't obviate the usefulness of being able to spend more Vitae to get it all done in one go. Is it strictly superior? No, and that's a good thing. It's a powerful option for when you need it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937224#post937224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you might lay out 5 shots and have them do 5 shots.. but why wouldn't you do 3 shots if they will have the same effect? Yes, I understand that sometimes 5 is needed, but 3 seems better all around. I also understand that is my perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>What? No, you have them do 1 shot with 5 Vitae in it instead of 3 shots with 1 Vitae each in them. That way by the time they've taken the first shot, they're already bonded, you don't have to risk them realizing that the drink they're shooting tastes funny and maybe this was a bad idea, or deciding one is enough, they're not 21 anymore, or any number of other reasons they might not take three shots.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937224#post937224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there anything else in WoD that makes you roll upon first taste to not be addicted? In college, took a class about OTC and Illegal drugs and the only drug ( that I remember.. it's been a while ) that you could get addicted to after the first hit was Ecstasy. Even heroine and Meth take repeated use... So if we equate vitae to the most addictive drug humans know... The only thing I can think of in wod that is more addicting... is Kiss of the Succubus..</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, how addictive it is is fairly moot, since as established above, even an addicted victim can refuse more, they just get the Deprived Condition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937224#post937224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I couldnt find the 3 nights thing, but I did find a couple people referencing the post...<br /> <br /> Ephsy, myself and Elderand seem to recall it too. ( I do hope we arent all crazy )</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, that's what I was able to find too. I'm pretty sure you guys are misremembering, because I can't find any post by Rose saying it has to be three separate nights, and it would be inconsistent with the text in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T14:28:50-07:00","id":937292,"title":"","content":"To be fair.. I havent given you a scenario, only examples.<br /> <br /> No scenario, setting time place plot all that was given because there are too many options. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T14:44:45-07:00","id":937303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937224#post937224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the arguments is that someone who had a spiked drink or food or whatever, Would not want to continue to drink or eat food because it tastes like coppery blood So it really does matter what it tastes like. most people do not turn down really really good tasting things.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm pretty sure that the argument is that people will identify the food tasting strange and stop eating, because they may suspect the food (or drink) has been tampered with. <br /> <br /> Pretend you're at a club - your drink suddenly tastes strange. Your first thought should be, &quot;Oh, hells. Someone just slipped something into my drink.&quot; It doesn't matter if the drink tastes better this way - warning flags in your head should be going off like mad. Now, does this happen with vitae instead of a regular drug? That is the arugment in question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If someone handed you a drink and you never had it before and it was the best thing you have ever tasted, strange or not. Why would you say no to round two? </div> </div> </div> Umm... I don't care if its the best thing I ever tasted. If I have the least bit of suspicion that someone might have dropped something in my drink, I'm ditching it. Got to keep yourself safe - no one else will. <br /> <br /> There are lots of reasons to say no. That's mine. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know that addiction is not mind control in anyway but you do have to roll a resolve comp NOT to take the drug again. </div> </div> </div> That's just vitae addiction rules specifically, not general drug rules, and you're slightly off with those rules.<br /> <br /> First, you don't even become Addicted until you miss your first Resolve + Composure roll (willpower may be spent). Nothing really happens beyond the first stage of a blood bond, and you might be leery of the drink now, if you have reason to be suspicious. There's nothing compelling you to drink more at this point. <br /> <br /> Second, even after you gain the Addicted Condition, you can choose one of three options - indulge, suceed on the Resolve + Composure roll, or take the Deprived Condition. At no point do you have to take the drug as the result of a failed roll. Its very likely you will, but its just as possible that we have the addict go Deprived, leave the room, get help, etc. Real life addictions are more than just physical dependacy on a substance. Its the ingraining of behavior patterns and mental dependacy. Tricking someone into becoming an addict won't immediately change their behavior patterns or force a mental dependacy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All that said. Many people seem to think that your victim will know what is happening to them. </div> </div> </div> Actually, the I'm thinking this: &quot;can a person become suspicious of a suddenly different tasting drink?&quot; At no point am I assuming the victim is aware. Only that they can detect a metalic taste, which could set flags depending on the person and situation in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T15:24:41-07:00","id":937329,"title":"","content":"the waitress comes to your table with a bunch of drinks, sets them down and says The man/woman over there bought these for you and your friends. You look over and he/she waves. it's a mixed drink you've never had before. vodka something and something with a little of that.<br /> <br /> Your coworker comes to you at your job and says, &quot;I just bought mochi for the first time, you gotta try this!&quot; the red gooey stuff in the center was delicious, was a little weird, but new. Why not another because it tasted really really good.<br /> <br /> Bob from down the street brings you coffee every day. He knows you hate your job and the perks of the caffeine are nice. today he tried some strange new flavor, but shit it was fantastic!<br /> <br /> The new guy at work brings everyone doughnuts on his first day. The strawberry jam in yours is mind blowing good, but a little different, maybe a new reciepe?<br /> <br /> The obfuscated vampire is sitting next to the waitress station and spiking all the drinks that go out. Remember this shit tastes really good really really good.<br /> <br /> have you never gone to a bar and ordered something new? Different? Tried new foods?<br /> <br /> If everyone could taste the roofies in their drinks.. no one would ever get roofied...<br /> If no one could taste the Valium in their food, no one would get drugged<br /> If everyone could taste the arsenic in their soup... no one would die of prolonged poisoning..<br /> <br /> I was just at the bar with my husband and a bunch of his coworkers. One of them bought us drinks. He came back to the table with something that looked like toilet bowl cleaner for me. We all laughed. I tried it. It was good. I said &quot;whats in this&quot; and kept drinking. My first thought wasnt.. Oh shit. i have never had this before it must be drugged...<br /> <br /> if the book says it tastes really really good... Why do people go to &quot;it must be drugged' And not just assume its a flavor you've never had before? There are literally thousands of types and ways to mix drinks and I doubt a normal person would be able to discern each contributing part. <br /> <br /> now like MCN said. if my drink suddenly tasted strange or different AFTER i drank half of it, then I would be worried, but if it started out different.. and good.. why would one assume that it is drugged?<br /> <br /> I am saying it's possible, but unlikely that someone would drink it and go &quot;ew that's blood&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 07-25-2016, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T15:41:33-07:00","id":937341,"title":"","content":"@MCN <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> <br /> <br /> Eh, it depends on what the drink is. If your having a GOOD margarita, your not going to taste anything metallic in it over the Tequila, if anything it might be more sweet thanks to the vitae. And after a few drinks most people don't really even notice the difference, how do you think people actually get drugged? Seriously, has nobody in this thread done much drinking? Your not going to taste much difference over more potent tastes, the vitae might shine through (the sweet taste), but not likely the blood, and in a sweet mixed drink that certainly won't stand out more than &quot;Wow, that is an awesome drink.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T17:56:29-07:00","id":937388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937329#post937329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the waitress comes to your table with a bunch of drinks, sets them down and says The man/woman over there bought these for you and your friends. You look over and he/she waves. it's a mixed drink you've never had before. vodka something and something with a little of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I'll try that. Care to tell me who the vampire is, how they got Vitae in this drink, why they want to blood bond me, and how they plan to get this to happen two more times? Cause right now this example doesn't look like it supports your position.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937329#post937329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your coworker comes to you at your job and says, &amp;quot;I just bought mochi for the first time, you gotta try this!&amp;quot; the red gooey stuff in the center was delicious, was a little weird, but new. Why not another because it tasted really really good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've had mochi before, and I think I would notice if the red stuff in the middle wasn't red bean paste. My coworker has some explaining to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937329#post937329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bob from down the street brings you coffee every day. He knows you hate your job and the perks of the caffeine are nice. today he tried some strange new flavor, but shit it was fantastic!</div> </div> </div> </div>He brought me a strange new flavor I didn't ask for? Thanks bob, but no. Just get me my usual next time unless I ask otherwise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937329#post937329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The new guy at work brings everyone doughnuts on his first day. The strawberry jam in yours is mind blowing good, but a little different, maybe a new reciepe?</div> </div> </div> </div>This new guy work the night shift, or is he somebody's thrall? What's his interest in blood bonding me when I just met him at work? What ever it is, he took a big risk here, and it didn't pay off because I don't like filled donughts. Guess he just accidentally got a one stage bond on some other random person at our work. Also, is he bringing donughts every day for three days straight?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937329#post937329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The obfuscated vampire is sitting next to the waitress station and spiking all the drinks that go out. Remember this shit tastes really good really really good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wh... Why? What possible interest could he have in getting a one stage blood bond with every random person who comes to this restaraunt?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937329#post937329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">have you never gone to a bar and ordered something new? Different? Tried new foods?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, on my own terms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937329#post937329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If everyone could taste the roofies in their drinks.. no one would ever get roofied...<br /> If no one could taste the Valium in their food, no one would get drugged<br /> If everyone could taste the arsenic in their soup... no one would die of prolonged poisoning..</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't even understand what your point is here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937329#post937329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was just at the bar with my husband and a bunch of his coworkers. One of them bought us drinks. He came back to the table with something that looked like toilet bowl cleaner for me. We all laughed. I tried it. It was good. I said &amp;quot;whats in this&amp;quot; and kept drinking. My first thought wasnt.. Oh shit. i have never had this before it must be drugged...</div> </div> </div> </div>Did anyone other than the you, bartender, or your husband handle the drink? If not then you probably had nothing to worry about. If so... Well, you're more bold than I would be in that situation, I guess?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937329#post937329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if the book says it tastes really really good... Why do people go to &amp;quot;it must be drugged' And not just assume its a flavor you've never had before? There are literally thousands of types and ways to mix drinks and I doubt a normal person would be able to discern each contributing part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because of the context of the discussion. We're talking about what the practical use of Voivode 3 is compared to just using a single point of Vitae 3 times when those times don't have to be on separate nights. I might try something that tastes a bit weird. I don't really see myself getting three of what ever it is in one night.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937329#post937329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">now like MCN said. if my drink suddenly tasted strange or different AFTER i drank half of it, then I would be worried, but if it started out different.. and good.. why would one assume that it is drugged?</div> </div> </div> </div>But would you then go and get two more? And how is the vampire in this scenario getting the Vitae in all three?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937329#post937329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am saying it's possible, but unlikely that someone would drink it and go &amp;quot;ew that's blood&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. It doesn't really matter if they would go &quot;ew that's blood.&quot; What matters is if there are scenarios where it would be more useful to go straight to 3rd stage bond in one go at the cost of more Vitae, rather than taking the time and effort to get them to drink your Vitae 3 times. Since Vitae is detectable by taste, and since you don't always have the time to wait around for three opportunities to get your blood in someone's body (by what ever means), yes, there is plenty of use for Voivode 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T18:18:55-07:00","id":937391,"title":"","content":"You don't get to know the vampire's reasons. If you knew everything behind the closed doors, the story would suck. Maybe you pissed off the nos and didn't even know it. Maybe the Daeva was looking for a door to open. He comes swooping in after you accept the first drink. Who cares the how or why. Maybe the ventrue dominated the waitress to let him spike. <br /> <br /> Second if bob was buying you coffee out of the Niceness of his heart and you told him to stuff it and bring you the usual. He would probably tell you to stuff it and not bring you coffee anymore. Period. That just seems like a dick move for someone who is just bringing you coffee to cheer you up. <br /> <br /> Yes. Like I said. The coworker brought the drinks to the table. I also don't think everyone is trying to drug me.<br /> <br /> I 100% agree with Rani. ( and that ties into my rant about if people could taste the poison no one would get poisoned ) The more potent taste is what you are going to be tasting. Especially after a few drinks.. People stop caring ... <br /> <br /> Anyway. I can see that the people in this argument are in &quot;no&quot; mode anyway. Tons of people don't even know what the hell mochi is... But you seem to assume that since you do everyone does, therefore no one would fall for that scenario...<br /> Even though I totally did that to my coworkers.. All these examples ( minus spiking the food ) I have done to get people to eat something.<br /> Bring coffee to a coworker I barely know, doughnuts to work for no reason, getting drinks or having drinks bought for me.. Usually people don't call me weird .. Or refuse seconds if they liked it. <br /> <br /> I think I am going to check out of this thread though as it's clearly not going anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T19:34:56-07:00","id":937412,"title":"","content":"@Rani - I can see an argument that it depends on the drink you get. But it also depends on how much blood goes in- remeber that vamps all have different ways to do this, and might be incapable of bonding with a single drop. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2308_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2308\" data-vbnamecard=\"2308\">Vitalis</a> - I certainly hope you know the vampire's motivation! You're playing the leech! This conversation is in the context of a PC using Voivode 3. Honestly, though, this is sounding more and more like a white room situation devode of context. If we're not bringing in the personalities and motives and Ambitions of the people involved, then its an unrealistic Exercise with no bearing on actual gameplay.<br /> <br /> EDIT - also, someone randomly dropping drinks at your table and accepting them is dangerous. Even if the drinks themselves are safe, too many people think you &quot;owe&quot; them something in return. Often sexual in nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-25-2016, 10:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T21:02:47-07:00","id":937454,"title":"","content":"Quick note: Vitae might feel good, but it tastes like blood. It might be the best blood you've ever tasted! It might do things to you you never knew blood could do! It might make you squirm with agonizing pleasure! But it's blood. It tastes like blood.<br /> <br /> As such, some of the examples are a little hrngh. Sure, you might get bonded, but you also probably know you just got blood. I mean, you might not if it was served with, say, tartare? But I'm gonna notice blood in my mochi. Blood doesn't go in mochi.<br /> <br /> EDIT: This is what I get for coming in at the tail end of a conversation-I say things that have already been said. Ignore me.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Though ,on the mochi example, what I'd do, even if it tasted good, is stop, think about it, and when it clicked, I'd ask if it was blood to the pertinent party. if they said yeah, sure, it was a thing? I'd swallow. If not? Uh. No. That's not a good route to go. That crosses my creepy line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-26-2016, 12:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T22:50:39-07:00","id":937489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937391#post937391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't get to know the vampire's reasons. If you knew everything behind the closed doors, the story would suck. Maybe you pissed off the nos and didn't even know it. Maybe the Daeva was looking for a door to open. He comes swooping in after you accept the first drink. Who cares the how or why. Maybe the ventrue dominated the waitress to let him spike.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know I wouldn't know these things if I was a player in a game where these things happened. But I'm not. I'm having a discussion on forums about the value of Voivode 3 under the &quot;different drinks don't have to be on different nights&quot; interpretation of the blood bond rules. And your scenarios don't make a very strong case for Voivode 3 not being useful if they're devoid of context.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937329#post937329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second if bob was buying you coffee out of the Niceness of his heart and you told him to stuff it and bring you the usual. He would probably tell you to stuff it and not bring you coffee anymore. Period. That just seems like a dick move for someone who is just bringing you coffee to cheer you up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say I would tell him to stuff it. I would politely decline. If he brought me a different drink without asking if I would like it and got upset that I didn't want it, that's on him. He didn't ask if I wanted this different drink. He doesn't know if I like the flavor, he doesn't know if I'm allergic to the ingredients. He took the risk of the offer being turned down when he decided to try to supprise me. And honestly, I'd appreciate the gesture, but I would still tell him I didn't want it, and I'd still ask him to check with me in the future before getting me something I didn't expect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937329#post937329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Like I said. The coworker brought the drinks to the table. I also don't think everyone is trying to drug me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's cool, you do you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937329#post937329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I 100% agree with Rani. ( and that ties into my rant about if people could taste the poison no one would get poisoned ) The more potent taste is what you are going to be tasting. Especially after a few drinks.. People stop caring ...</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, you can taste Vitae. It explicitly has a distinctive flavor, and as per one of the examples, it's a flavor that is noticable in coffee. You can't taste a lot of common date rape drugs, which is part of why they're used. So from where I'm standing that rant seems inconsistent with your position in this discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937329#post937329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway. I can see that the people in this argument are in &quot;no&quot; mode anyway. Tons of people don't even know what the hell mochi is... But you seem to assume that since you do everyone does, therefore no one would fall for that scenario...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry you feel that way. And no, I don't assume everyone has tried mochi, but your scenarios were presented in second person so I responded to them in first person. And if this vampire is counting on his victim not having tried mochi before, he'd better do his research if he doesn't want his plan foiled by someone who was way too into anime in high school.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937329#post937329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even though I totally did that to my coworkers.. All these examples ( minus spiking the food ) I have done to get people to eat something.<br /> Bring coffee to a coworker I barely know, doughnuts to work for no reason, getting drinks or having drinks bought for me.. Usually people don't call me weird .. Or refuse seconds if they liked it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. But like, what you've done in real life doesnt make a compelling argument for Voivode 3 not being useful under my interpretation of the blood bonding rules. I mean, I'll concede that it's not <i>that</i> hard to get people to consume something more than once. But that doesn't change the fact that there are plenty of scenarios in which it would be more beneficial to get to that third stage bond all in one go, even at the cost of more Vitae. One of which is if your intended victim is aware of the taste and properties of Vitae. And another of which is if your intended victim is especially cautious about accepting food or drinks from people they don't know well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937329#post937329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I am going to check out of this thread though as it's clearly not going anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I'm sorry you feel that way. It's not my intent to shut down discussion or chase you away. It just seems like your arguments are drifting further and further away from the point of contention (the utility of Voivode 3) and I'm trying to address your points while also bringing it back to the topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-26-2016, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T07:21:06-07:00","id":937585,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a><br /> <br /> You're right we are getting off topic. Cause and effect. Someone says it tastes like blood and We respond with the book says it is subtle, strange and tastes like dessert wine, but we all seem to ignore that. Like if we add velveeta cheese into chocolate fudge ( yes i have had this ) it is really good fudge, but you would never know there is velveeta cheese in there, even though Velveeta cheese is super potent and has a unique flavor of it's own.<br /> <br /> <br /> So when you assume that even if you put a little vitae in a glass of (for example ) Vodka, grenadine, and sprite, pineapple juice, orange juice and creamer that everyone will be like &quot;yup there is blood in here, eww..&quot; The Coil is going to be pretty high in demand, In the case where you can 100% all the time, when everyone know that they are tasting blood. If you play that way. you're right. The Coil is totally necessary. My argument was that.. it's super subtle. That it might taste different, strange, but it tastes AMAZING. &quot;really really good&quot; as per book. so if you dropped it into a mixed drink or a shot, it would blend mix.. and become new flavor.. especially with Alcohol, that will be what kicks above the &quot;sweet dessert wine&quot; flavor. I dont think the subtle coppery taste would be the first thing people noticed. I said I would give an occult roll for people in the know to well.. know.<br /> <br /> Also most people have not drank blood before so even if there is a strange slightly coppery taste it still does taste really sweet and really really good and we should remember that. Sure if they handed you a shot of pure vitae.. I might look at this thick syrupy liquid that smells strange I might question it. Most people would, but when Mixed with something, I dont think it becomes the most potent thing.<br /> <br /> Real life shows what a good baseline should be for your NPCs. If it is possible to get your coworkers to try strange new foods they have never had before. Or if it is possible to get someone to drink something at a bar, then it should be a possibility in game. It shouldnt be cast aside as a &quot;that wouldnt work&quot; All my scenarios were second person, because i was talking about the general plural &quot;you&quot; not the specific you. You answered as a player, as the victim, victims dont generally get to know why it is happening.<br /> <br /> I couldnt help myself. I made a survey and posted it on Facebook about this ( and the one night stand thing from the majesty thread )<br /> The question was like &quot;Someone gives you food/drink and it tastes really really good, but there is something odd and its unlike anything you have had before, What is your first thought?&quot; 22 out of 23 people said they would &quot;What's in this? Can I have another?&quot; the other 1 picked &quot;that's odd. no way do I want more&quot; and the 3rd option which no one picked was &quot;It's drugged&quot; not a single person thought that their drink was drugged. I left the someone vague because it could be a waitress, or a coworker, or a friend, or neighbor or a stranger. I know that most people were probably thinking it is someone they know... but Why cant they know this vampire who is trying to spike them? ( or at least have them charmed or socially maneuvered to the friendly stage )<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2102_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2102\" data-vbnamecard=\"2102\">MCN</a> rarely are the drinks random. You can usually tell if someone is trying to make friends or sexual advances. That is a very common attempt, you buy someone a drink, then you drink it and they come over and talk to you. perhaps offer to buy you a second or third.<br /> As for the drinks, yes it depends on the drink, but even if you put Vitae in someone's coke, I think maybe it would be a not normal flavor of coke as you can literally add hundreds of different types of syrup to it to make different cokes.<br /> If we are talking a human... every vampire can bond in a single go. Human's are not able to resist this ability.<br /> Everything changes if we are talking a kindred as all the spiking food and drinks goes out the window.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> It does make you feel good and it tastes &quot;really really good&quot; &quot;dessert wine&quot; as per book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 07-26-2016, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T08:14:27-07:00","id":937611,"title":"","content":"Also assuming that a Kindred is Staked. And you pour blood in his mouth. Can this count towards forming a blood bond? Can the Staked Kindred resist the bond while staked?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11988-montgomery-crobes","name":"Montgomery Crobes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T08:44:25-07:00","id":937627,"title":"","content":"I would say yes on both accounts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T08:56:12-07:00","id":937630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937585#post937585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're right we are getting off topic. Cause and effect. Someone says it tastes like blood and We respond with the book says it is subtle, strange and tastes like dessert wine, but we all seem to ignore that. Like if we add velveeta cheese into chocolate fudge ( yes i have had this ) it is really good fudge, but you would never know there is velveeta cheese in there, even though Velveeta cheese is super potent and has a unique flavor of it's own.<br /> <br /> So when you assume that even if you put a little vitae in a glass of (for example ) Vodka, grenadine, and sprite, pineapple juice, orange juice and creamer that everyone will be like &quot;yup there is blood in here, eww..&quot; The Coil is going to be pretty high in demand, In the case where you can 100% all the time, when everyone know that they are tasting blood. If you play that way. you're right. The Coil is totally necessary. My argument was that.. it's super subtle. That it might taste different, strange, but it tastes AMAZING. &quot;really really good&quot; as per book. so if you dropped it into a mixed drink or a shot, it would blend mix.. and become new flavor.. especially with Alcohol, that will be what kicks above the &quot;sweet dessert wine&quot; flavor. I dont think the subtle coppery taste would be the first thing people noticed. I said I would give an occult roll for people in the know to well.. know.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a serious misrepresentation of my argument. I never said it would be 100% detectible all the time. It is, as per an example in the book, detectible in coffee. And frankly? Even if it was 0% detectable, you could never tell, Voivode 3 would <i>still</i> have uses, because putting Vitae into food and drink is not the only way to blood bond someone, and moreover you just don't always have the time or the opportunity to deliver the Vitae three separate times. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937329#post937329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also most people have not drank blood before so even if there is a strange slightly coppery taste it still does taste really sweet and really really good and we should remember that. Sure if they handed you a shot of pure vitae.. I might look at this thick syrupy liquid that smells strange I might question it. Most people would, but when Mixed with something, I dont think it becomes the most potent thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's impossible to get someone to try something they haven't before, so I really don't know what you're trying to prove here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937329#post937329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Real life shows what a good baseline should be for your NPCs. If it is possible to get your coworkers to try strange new foods they have never had before. Or if it is possible to get someone to drink something at a bar, then it should be a possibility in game. It shouldnt be cast aside as a &quot;that wouldnt work&quot; All my scenarios were second person, because i was talking about the general plural &quot;you&quot; not the specific you. You answered as a player, as the victim, victims dont generally get to know why it is happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and I answered without context, because as a player I wouldn't have it. Then I challenged the plausibility of some of your scenarios actually occurring in-game, and asked you to contextualize them and your response was &quot;you don't know.&quot; I know I don't know, that's why I answered without knowing. But again, if you can't demonstrate how the scenario has relevance to the game we're discussing then it doesn't support your argument. Unless your argument is just &quot;it's possible to get people to try new things&quot;, which I don't disagree with, have no interest in disputing, and doesn't obviate the usefulness of Voivode 3.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937329#post937329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I couldnt help myself. I made a survey and posted it on Facebook about this ( and the one night stand thing from the majesty thread )<br /> The question was like &quot;Someone gives you food/drink and it tastes really really good, but there is something odd and its unlike anything you have had before, What is your first thought?&quot; 22 out of 23 people said they would &quot;What's in this? Can I have another?&quot; the other 1 picked &quot;that's odd. no way do I want more&quot; and the 3rd option which no one picked was &quot;It's drugged&quot; not a single person thought that their drink was drugged. I left the someone vague because it could be a waitress, or a coworker, or a friend, or neighbor or a stranger. I know that most people were probably thinking it is someone they know... but Why cant they know this vampire who is trying to spike them? ( or at least have them charmed or socially maneuvered to the friendly stage )</div> </div> </div> </div>O... Kay...? You're really going a long way to prove a point I have already conceded. Yes, there are scenarios in which a person would accept food or drink containing Vitae and not become suspicious. That doesn't mean there aren't scenarios in which someone would accept food or drink containing Vitae and become suspicious, and this is supported by your one person polled who said they wouldn't want the thing again. And even if there weren't? That's <i>still</i> not the only reason Voivode 3 is useful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937329#post937329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we are talking a human... every vampire can bond in a single go. Human's are not able to resist this ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans don't get a roll to resist the bond, but they still have to drink on three separate occasions to get to a third stage bond.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937329#post937329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything changes if we are talking a kindred as all the spiking food and drinks goes out the window.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, look at that. A whole group of people whom Voivode 3 is useful in attempting to blood bond.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-26-2016, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T15:53:48-07:00","id":937809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=936253#post936253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2\" data-vbnamecard=\"2\">Rose Bailey</a> So, which is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can do it in one night. I'd say not one scene or even one hour, though. It takes some time to metaphysically &quot;digest.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's <i>possible</i> I said otherwise at one point, but this is what's in my notes, and it's how I've run it in the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T06:50:10-07:00","id":938074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=937585#post937585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also most people have not drank blood before [snip]</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun fact: Nearly everyone has tasted blood at one time or another. The most likely candidate for when you first did was when you lost your baby teeth. Not saying I agree or disagree with any of the arguments in this thread, just pointing this out.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T07:36:42-07:00","id":938102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=938074#post938074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fun fact: Nearly everyone has tasted blood at one time or another. The most likely candidate for when you first did was when you lost your baby teeth. Not saying I agree or disagree with any of the arguments in this thread, just pointing this out.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for that.. if I put the amount of blood i tasted in a glass of vodka or into a cupcake.. I would NEVER know it was there. By drank I meant drank a glass or a shot or a large quantity, not &quot;tasted&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T08:09:54-07:00","id":938116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=938102#post938102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for that.. if I put the amount of blood i tasted in a glass of vodka or into a cupcake.. I would NEVER know it was there. By drank I meant drank a glass or a shot or a large quantity, not &quot;tasted&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, someone more used to the taste (a boxer/MMA fighter, or someone just really clumsy) might immediately be able to figure out what it is.<br /> <br /> Edit: For the record, my personal opinion on the matter -- How difficult Blood-Bonding someone is should be dependent on the story. Random Joe from the bar, and who isn't likely to become an important factor in the Chronicle? Sure, three spiked shots and he's yours. The Prince's mortal descendent (and Touchstone)? You're going to have to work for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4854,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","user":"Justin Sane","date":". 07-27-2016, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T08:42:09-07:00","id":938135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=938116#post938116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, someone more used to the taste (a boxer/MMA fighter, or someone just really clumsy) might immediately be able to figure out what it is.<br /> <br /> Edit: For the record, my personal opinion on the matter -- How difficult Blood-Bonding someone is should be dependent on the story. Random Joe from the bar, and who isn't likely to become an important factor in the Chronicle? Sure, three spiked shots and he's yours. The Prince's mortal descendent (and Touchstone)? You're going to have to work for it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> With what Rose said, 3 shots in a bar wont work. You need more time between and that was my thought all along. ( I thought 3 nights, but she is saying at least hours ) Which makes the coil super good, back to what I thought it was anyway. <br /> <br /> ( &quot;most people&quot; arent MMA fighters either )<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T10:10:30-07:00","id":938185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/936031-blood-bonds-2e?p=938116#post938116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, someone more used to the taste (a boxer/MMA fighter, or someone just really clumsy) might immediately be able to figure out what it is.<br /> <br /> Edit: For the record, my personal opinion on the matter -- How difficult Blood-Bonding someone is should be dependent on the story. Random Joe from the bar, and who isn't likely to become an important factor in the Chronicle? Sure, three spiked shots and he's yours. The Prince's mortal descendent (and Touchstone)? You're going to have to work for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a more nuanced scheme for determining the amount of exposure it takes to forge a blood bond would be cool. In-character, they actually have a huge amount of variation, but I didn't want to bog things down with mechanics and tracking requirements in the core. Especially since for a lot of groups blood bonds are an off-screen thing done before the game, rather than a frequently-used tool during the action.<br /> <br /> You could rip out the whole existing system and do it as an extended action or social maneuver sequence. That works more if you're using blood bonds as a metaphor for or extension of gaining someone's trust, rather than as cheap-but-messy mind control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}